    "id": "madas/as-pure-c/q12",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/as-pure-c/q12-question-1.svg\" alt=\"A population P of an endangered species of animals was introduced to a park. The population obeys the equation t 125 ka P t , 0 , = ≥ t k 2 a + where k and a are positive constants, and t is the time in years since the species was introduced to the park . Initially 100 individual animals were introduced to the park, and this population doubled after 5 years. a) Show that k = 8 . 2 ( )\" style=\"--madas-width:573.3px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/as-pure-c/q12-question-2.svg\" alt=\"3 b) Find the value of a , correct to 4 significant figures. ( ) 6 c) Determine the value of t when the P = 400 . ( ) d) Explain why this population cannot exceed 500. 3 ( )\" style=\"--madas-width:573.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/as-pure-c/q12-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"The population is 𝑃= 125𝑘𝑎𝑡/(𝑘+2𝑎𝑡). The time 𝑡is measured in years. At 𝑡= 0, 𝑃= 100, and at 𝑡= 5, 𝑃= 200. (a) Use the initial values: 100 = 125𝑘𝑎0 𝑘+ 2𝑎0 = 125𝑘 [M1] 𝑘+ 2 100(𝑘+ 2) = 125𝑘 100𝑘+ 200 = 125𝑘 [A1] 200 = 25𝑘, 𝑘= 8 . (b) Use 𝑡= 5 and 𝑃= 200 in the revised formula: 𝑃= 125 × 8 × 𝑎𝑡 8 + 2𝑎𝑡\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/as-pure-c/q12-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"200 = 125 × 8 × 𝑎5 = 1000𝑎5 [M1] 8 + 2𝑎5 8 + 2𝑎5 5𝑎5 1 = 8 + 2𝑎5 8 + 2𝑎5 = 5𝑎5, [A1] 8 = 3𝑎5 5√8 [A1] 𝑎= 3 = 1.216728 … ≈1.217 . (c) Use the revised expression and retain the unrounded value of 𝑎. 𝑃= 1000𝑎𝑡 8 + 2𝑎𝑡= 500𝑎𝑡 [M1] 4 + 𝑎𝑡 400 = 500𝑎𝑡 [M1] 4 + 𝑎𝑡 5𝑎𝑡 4 = 4 + 𝑎𝑡\" style=\"--madas-width:564.0px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/as-pure-c/q12-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"[A1] 16 + 4𝑎𝑡= 5𝑎𝑡, 16 = 𝑎𝑡 log 16 = log 𝑎𝑡= 𝑡log 𝑎 [M1] 𝑡= log 16 log 16 [A1] log 𝑎= log(1.2167 …) = 14.1339 … ≈14.13 years . [A1] (d) Divide numerator and denominator by 𝑎𝑡. 𝑃= 1000𝑎𝑡 8 + 2𝑎𝑡= 500𝑎𝑡 500 [M1] 4 + 𝑎𝑡= 4/𝑎𝑡+ 1. As 𝑡increases, 𝑎𝑡becomes arbitrarily large since 𝑎&gt; 1. Thus 4/𝑎𝑡approaches zero. [B1] It remains positive for every finite 𝑡, so the population starts at 100 and approaches its limiting value of 500 from below. Hence 𝑃&lt; 500 . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 12 is 14 marks.</p>"
    ],
